1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,724
Hello! Today I'm your guide.

2
00:00:01,724 --> 00:00:05,542
Let's travel together from Incheon Airport to Gangnam Station.

3
00:00:05,542 --> 00:00:08,498
We'll take a bus, ride the subway, and transfer.

4
00:00:08,498 --> 00:00:11,330
After this video, you won't get lost in Seoul!

5
00:00:17,850 --> 00:00:22,111
The first thought when you land: 'How do I get to Seoul'?

6
00:00:22,111 --> 00:00:25,400
There's one magic phrase for this: '어떻게 가요'?

7
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:26,970
— How do I get there?

8
00:00:31,690 --> 00:00:36,484
Add your destination: '서울까지 어떻게 가요'?

9
00:00:36,484 --> 00:00:41,278
The word '까지' marks the destination.

10
00:00:41,278 --> 00:00:45,540
You can swap it: '강남역까지 어떻게 가요'?

11
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:52,485
Today's key verb: '타다' — to ride, to take.

12
00:00:52,485 --> 00:00:57,639
버스를 타요 (take a bus). 지하철을 타요 (take the subway).

13
00:00:57,639 --> 00:01:00,380
One verb covers them all.

14
00:01:00,880 --> 00:01:04,632
There are two main ways from the airport to Seoul: bus and subway.

15
00:01:04,632 --> 00:01:05,940
Today we'll learn both.

16
00:01:09,470 --> 00:01:10,358
First, the bus.

17
00:01:10,358 --> 00:01:13,140
The airport bus is great when you have luggage.

18
00:01:13,140 --> 00:01:14,324
You sit comfortably,

19
00:01:14,324 --> 00:01:16,810
and your bags go in the compartment below.

20
00:01:20,620 --> 00:01:25,403
The place you catch a bus is '정류장' (bus stop).

21
00:01:25,403 --> 00:01:29,770
Just outside the airport you'll find them.

22
00:01:29,770 --> 00:01:31,850
Ask: '버스 정류장이 어디예요'?

23
00:01:35,490 --> 00:01:38,558
Korean buses are identified by number.

24
00:01:38,558 --> 00:01:42,190
So you ask: '몇 번 버스예요'? (Which bus number? ).

25
00:01:42,190 --> 00:01:45,500
Know the number, and you can go anywhere.

26
00:01:46,620 --> 00:01:49,179
To ask about time: '얼마나 걸려요'?

27
00:01:49,179 --> 00:01:51,473
(How long does it take? ).

28
00:01:51,473 --> 00:01:55,620
Buses can be delayed by traffic, so always ask.

29
00:01:59,050 --> 00:02:02,645
The fare is '요금'. Ask: '요금이 얼마예요'?

30
00:02:02,645 --> 00:02:05,289
(How much is the fare? ).

31
00:02:05,289 --> 00:02:10,470
The airport bus costs a bit more than the subway.

32
00:02:12,460 --> 00:02:15,631
But today we'll take the subway. Why?

33
00:02:15,631 --> 00:02:18,288
It never gets stuck in traffic,

34
00:02:18,288 --> 00:02:21,630
so the time is exact. '빨라요' means fast.

35
00:02:24,890 --> 00:02:28,542
'지하철' — the subway, a train that runs underground.

36
00:02:28,542 --> 00:02:32,633
The one from the airport is called the Airport Railroad.

37
00:02:32,633 --> 00:02:33,290
Let's go!

38
00:02:36,260 --> 00:02:40,116
But there's a problem! To ride, you need a card.

39
00:02:40,116 --> 00:02:42,366
Without it you can't get in.

40
00:02:42,366 --> 00:02:45,740
This card is called '교통카드' (transit card).

41
00:02:50,220 --> 00:02:55,259
Don't worry — you can buy one at a convenience store or machine.

42
00:02:55,259 --> 00:02:58,880
Just say: '교통카드 주세요' (A transit card, please).

43
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:08,554
Once you have the card, you must put money in.

44
00:03:08,554 --> 00:03:12,050
That's '충전' — to top up, to charge the card.

45
00:03:15,670 --> 00:03:20,481
Say it with an amount: '만 원 충전해 주세요' (Please top up 10,

46
00:03:20,481 --> 00:03:24,768
000 won). One card works for both subway and bus.

47
00:03:24,768 --> 00:03:25,730
Very handy.

48
00:03:26,580 --> 00:03:27,989
Now the gate.

49
00:03:27,989 --> 00:03:32,108
Lightly touch your card to the reader.

50
00:03:32,108 --> 00:03:37,310
That's '대다' — to tap. '카드를 대세요' (Tap your card).

51
00:03:39,030 --> 00:03:42,368
'Beep'! — and you're through. The gate opens.

52
00:03:42,368 --> 00:03:44,890
Success! Now down to the platform.

53
00:03:49,630 --> 00:03:50,739
On the platform,

54
00:03:50,739 --> 00:03:53,998
another puzzle: there are two directions. Left?

55
00:03:53,998 --> 00:03:55,800
Right? Which way do we go?

56
00:04:00,540 --> 00:04:02,672
So many travelers make a mistake here.

57
00:04:02,672 --> 00:04:06,208
Take the wrong direction and you have to come all the way back.

58
00:04:06,208 --> 00:04:07,330
A big waste of time.

59
00:04:11,530 --> 00:04:15,357
Trains are marked with '행' (bound for).

60
00:04:15,357 --> 00:04:19,969
'서울역행' means the train bound for Seoul Station.

61
00:04:19,969 --> 00:04:22,520
Look for your destination.

62
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:28,157
Still unsure? Just ask: '이거 서울역 가요'?

63
00:04:28,157 --> 00:04:30,988
(Does this go to Seoul Station? ).

64
00:04:30,988 --> 00:04:35,650
This phrase is your lifeline — Koreans will gladly help.

65
00:04:36,820 --> 00:04:42,262
'네, 맞아요' — Yes, that's right. Now you can relax.

66
00:04:42,262 --> 00:04:47,930
If they say '아니요' (no), just go to the other side.

67
00:04:49,340 --> 00:04:50,904
The doors open — get on.

68
00:04:50,904 --> 00:04:54,620
But let people off first; that's the polite way in Korea.

69
00:04:57,180 --> 00:04:57,846
No seat?

70
00:04:57,846 --> 00:05:02,672
Stand and hold the '손잡이' (strap) hanging from the ceiling.

71
00:05:02,672 --> 00:05:06,250
You'll be steady even when the train rocks.

72
00:05:08,170 --> 00:05:12,218
How far is it? Ask '몇 정거장이에요'? (How many stops? ).

73
00:05:12,218 --> 00:05:17,480
And listen to the announcements — they call out the next station.

74
00:05:20,720 --> 00:05:22,546
We've arrived at Seoul Station.

75
00:05:22,546 --> 00:05:26,670
But this isn't Gangnam yet — here we must change to a different train.

76
00:05:29,550 --> 00:05:33,973
Today's most important word: '환승' — transfer.

77
00:05:33,973 --> 00:05:38,101
Changing to a different line is called 환승.

78
00:05:38,101 --> 00:05:39,870
Remember this one!

79
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:45,522
'환승하다' and '갈아타다' mean the same thing.

80
00:05:45,522 --> 00:05:49,398
'2호선으로 갈아타요' (Change to Line 2).

81
00:05:49,398 --> 00:05:54,000
Both are common — learn them together.

82
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:57,780
Transfer corridors are huge — many signs,

83
00:05:57,780 --> 00:06:00,538
many people. It's easy to get confused.

84
00:06:00,538 --> 00:06:01,740
So what do we do?

85
00:06:05,720 --> 00:06:09,902
Just ask! '어디서 갈아타요'? (Where do I transfer? ).

86
00:06:09,902 --> 00:06:14,720
Ask a station staff member or the person next to you.

87
00:06:16,010 --> 00:06:22,625
Subway lines are called by number: 1호선, 2호선,

88
00:06:22,625 --> 00:06:29,690
3호선 (Line 1, 2, 3). '호선' means the line number.

89
00:06:31,630 --> 00:06:34,762
Gangnam Station is on Line 2.

90
00:06:34,762 --> 00:06:38,758
So: '2호선으로 갈아타세요' (Change to Line 2).

91
00:06:38,758 --> 00:06:40,270
Let's find it.

92
00:06:46,940 --> 00:06:49,255
Here's a tip! Each line has a color.

93
00:06:49,255 --> 00:06:50,284
Line 2 is green.

94
00:06:50,284 --> 00:06:52,535
Even if you can't read the letters,

95
00:06:52,535 --> 00:06:53,950
just follow the color.

96
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,701
Now follow the green signs.

97
00:06:59,701 --> 00:07:01,214
The arrows show the way.

98
00:07:01,214 --> 00:07:03,860
Watch the signs and you'll never get lost.

99
00:07:06,830 --> 00:07:10,901
We did it! We've reached the Line 2 platform.

100
00:07:10,901 --> 00:07:14,610
That's what 환승 means. Not so hard, right?

101
00:07:17,500 --> 00:07:19,905
Now we ride Line 2 to Gangnam Station.

102
00:07:19,905 --> 00:07:22,437
You can see the city through the window.

103
00:07:22,437 --> 00:07:23,260
Almost there!

104
00:07:28,320 --> 00:07:34,939
The opposite of '타다' is '내리다' (to get off).

105
00:07:34,939 --> 00:07:39,864
타다 / 내리다 — learn them as a pair.

106
00:07:39,864 --> 00:07:44,020
'여기서 내려요' (I get off here).

107
00:07:44,470 --> 00:07:45,528
One last problem!

108
00:07:45,528 --> 00:07:47,707
Gangnam Station has a LOT of exits.

109
00:07:47,707 --> 00:07:50,570
Take the wrong one and you'll walk a long way.

110
00:07:52,650 --> 00:07:56,619
So ask: '몇 번 출구예요'? (Which exit number? ).

111
00:07:56,619 --> 00:07:57,470
In Korea,

112
00:07:57,470 --> 00:08:03,140
people meet by exit number: 'Let's meet at Gangnam Exit 11'.

113
00:08:05,480 --> 00:08:09,231
'11번 출구요' — Exit 11. They answer with a number.

114
00:08:09,231 --> 00:08:13,540
Climb the stairs and you're on the streets of Gangnam!

115
00:08:13,990 --> 00:08:14,696
Final tip!

116
00:08:14,696 --> 00:08:18,013
You can also transfer from the subway to a bus.

117
00:08:18,013 --> 00:08:21,260
Just tap the same transit card. So convenient!

118
00:08:24,740 --> 00:08:32,548
Let's review: 버스 (bus), 지하철 (subway), 타다 (ride),

119
00:08:32,548 --> 00:08:39,055
환승 (transfer), 내리다 (get off), 출구 (exit).

120
00:08:39,055 --> 00:08:46,050
These six words take you anywhere in Seoul.

121
00:08:46,500 --> 00:08:47,990
We made it to Gangnam!

122
00:08:47,990 --> 00:08:51,377
We traveled all the way from the airport together.

123
00:08:51,377 --> 00:08:54,560
Next time: asking for directions. See you then!

